{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q421814","formula":"Mg₃Al₂(SiO₄)₃","hill":"Al2Mg3O12Si3","elements":["O","Mg","Al","Si"],"composition":{"O":12.0,"Al":2.0,"Mg":3.0,"Si":3.0},"names":{"en":"Pyrope","ru":"Пироп","uk":"Піроп"},"descriptions":{"en":"The mineral pyrope is a member of the garnet group. Pyrope is the only member of the garnet family to always display red colouration in natural samples, and it is from this characteristic that it gets its name: from the Greek words for fire and eye. Despite being less common than most garnets, it is a widely used gemstone with numerous alternative names, some of which are misnomers.","ru":"Пиро́п (от др.-греч. πυρωπός — подобный огню) — минерал, силикат из группы гранатов. Встречается в кимберлитах (вместе с алмазами) и других ультраосновных горных породах.","uk":"Піроп — розповсюджений мінерал класу силікатів групи ґранатів, магніїсто-глиноземистий силікат острівної будови."},"fame":33,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-6073","atoms":203,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[11.571,0.0,0.0],[0.0,11.571,0.0],[0.0,0.0,11.571]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":2.893,"z":1.446,"el":"Mg"},{"x":11.571,"y":2.893,"z":1.446,"el":"Mg"},{"x":10.125,"y":5.786,"z":2.893,"el":"Mg"},{"x":1.446,"y":0.0,"z":2.893,"el":"Mg"},{"x":1.446,"y":11.571,"z":2.893,"el":"Mg"},{"x":2.893,"y":1.446,"z":0.0,"el":"Mg"},{"x":2.893,"y":1.446,"z":11.571,"el":"Mg"},{"x":2.893,"y":10.125,"z":5.786,"el":"Mg"},{"x":5.786,"y":2.893,"z":10.125,"el":"Mg"},{"x":5.786,"y":2.893,"z":4.339,"el":"Mg"},{"x":7.232,"y":0.0,"z":2.893,"el":"Mg"},{"x":7.232,"y":11.571,"z":2.893,"el":"Mg"},{"x":4.339,"y":5.786,"z":2.893,"el":"Mg"},{"x":2.893,"y":4.339,"z":5.786,"el":"Mg"},{"x":2.893,"y":7.232,"z":0.0,"e